A||N||1||Hawker||Headlight problems||||3||
Z||000000||Hawker||08-02-2001||06:20 PM||||Help, Please! My 86 GT has developed headlamp problems. If you push the switch all the way in, the lights come on but they will not rise up. If you just barely touch the switch, they come up and will stay up when the switch is pushed in fully. They go down fine. I had this problem last year and replaced the switch and this cured things. Now it's doing it again and a new switch does not help. Could it be the isolation relay? Any help is very, very welcom||||reg||3
Z||000001||StuGood||08-02-2001||06:36 PM||||Yes, I think it could be.  If your car has been eating light switch contacts, maybe the freewheeling diode around the isolation relay's coil is open, and failing to do its job of protecting the light switch's "headlights up" (yellow wire) contacts.<P>That's what you were thinking, right?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Incidentally, I've never seen it happen before, but I'm thinking it could.  Even though diodes are pretty reliable. <P>Don't forget to try the simple stuff first, like making sure the connector in back of the light switch is in good shape and making good contact, etc.   Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
